# React Native Standards for BookRentNew

## Component Structure

### Functional Components
Always use functional components with hooks:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

export default function BookCard({ book, onPress }) {
  const [isFavorite, setIsFavorite] = useState(false);
  
  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>{book.title}</Text>
    </View>
  );
}

// ❌ BAD - Avoid class components
class BookCard extends React.Component {
  render() {
    return <View>...</View>;
  }
}
```

### PropTypes and Defaults
Always validate props:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
export default function RentModal({ book, visible = false, onClose }) {
  if (!book) return null;
  // ... component code
}

// ❌ BAD - No prop validation
export default function RentModal(props) {
  return <View>{props.book.title}</View>;
}
```

## State Management

### Local State with useState
For component-level state:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const [books, setBooks] = useState([]);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
const [error, setError] = useState(null);

// Update state immutably
setBooks([...books, newBook]);

// ❌ BAD - Mutating state
books.push(newBook);
setBooks(books);
```

### Side Effects with useEffect
Handle side effects properly:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
useEffect(() => {
  const fetchBooks = async () => {
    try {
      setLoading(true);
      const data = await getBooks();
      setBooks(data);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err.message);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  };
  
  fetchBooks();
}, []);

// ❌ BAD - Missing cleanup or dependencies
useEffect(() => {
  fetchBooks();
});
```

## Navigation

### React Navigation Patterns
Use consistent navigation patterns:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const handleBookPress = (book) => {
  navigation.navigate('BookDetails', { 
    bookId: book.id,
    book: book 
  });
};

// Access params in destination screen
const { bookId, book } = route.params;

// ❌ BAD - Passing too much data
navigation.navigate('BookDetails', { 
  entireDatabase: database 
});
```

## Styling

### StyleSheet API
Always use StyleSheet.create():

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    padding: 16,
    backgroundColor: '#ffffff',
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: 18,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
    color: '#333',
  },
});

// ❌ BAD - Inline styles for everything
<View style={{ padding: 10, margin: 5, flex: 1 }}>
```

### Responsive Design
Use Dimensions or percentage-based sizing:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { Dimensions } from 'react-native';
const { width, height } = Dimensions.get('window');

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: {
    width: width * 0.9,
    height: height * 0.3,
  },
});

// ❌ BAD - Fixed pixel values
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: {
    width: 350,
    height: 200,
  },
});
```

## Error Handling

### Try-Catch Blocks
Always handle errors gracefully:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
const handleRentBook = async (bookId) => {
  try {
    setLoading(true);
    await rentBook(bookId);
    Alert.alert('Success', 'Book rented successfully!');
    navigation.goBack();
  } catch (error) {
    Alert.alert('Error', error.message || 'Failed to rent book');
    console.error('Rent book error:', error);
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};

// ❌ BAD - No error handling
const handleRentBook = async (bookId) => {
  await rentBook(bookId);
  navigation.goBack();
};
```

## Performance

### Optimize Re-renders
Use React.memo and useCallback:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { memo, useCallback } from 'react';

const BookCard = memo(({ book, onPress }) => {
  const handlePress = useCallback(() => {
    onPress(book.id);
  }, [book.id, onPress]);
  
  return (
    <TouchableOpacity onPress={handlePress}>
      <Text>{book.title}</Text>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
});

// ❌ BAD - Re-creates function on every render
const BookCard = ({ book, onPress }) => {
  return (
    <TouchableOpacity onPress={() => onPress(book.id)}>
      <Text>{book.title}</Text>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
};
```

### FlatList for Long Lists
Always use FlatList or SectionList for lists:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
<FlatList
  data={books}
  renderItem={({ item }) => <BookCard book={item} />}
  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id.toString()}
  initialNumToRender={10}
  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}
  windowSize={5}
/>

// ❌ BAD - Mapping arrays in ScrollView
<ScrollView>
  {books.map(book => <BookCard key={book.id} book={book} />)}
</ScrollView>
```

## Code Organization

### File Structure
- **Screens**: Full-page components in `/src/screens/`
- **Components**: Reusable UI components in `/src/components/`
- **Navigation**: Navigation setup in `/src/navigation/`
- **Utils**: Helper functions and constants

### Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `BookCard.js`)
- Functions: camelCase (e.g., `handleBookPress`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `API_BASE_URL`)
- Files: Match component name (e.g., `BookCard.js` for BookCard component)

## Expo Specific

### Asset Management
Use Expo's asset system:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { Image } from 'react-native';
<Image 
  source={require('./assets/book-placeholder.png')} 
  style={styles.image}
/>

// For remote images, add caching
<Image 
  source={{ uri: book.coverUrl, cache: 'force-cache' }}
  defaultSource={require('./assets/book-placeholder.png')}
/>
```

### Safe Area
Always handle safe areas:

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';

export default function HomeScreen() {
  return (
    <SafeAreaView style={styles.container}>
      {/* Content */}
    </SafeAreaView>
  );
}
```
